c016 back: No, unless ρ = 1. Under Assumption 2.0 with d > 0 and 0 < ρ ≤ 1, at stage n it is (1 − (1 − ρ)^(n+1))/ρ, which is smaller than 1/ρ at every finite n when ρ < 1. When ρ = 1 it equals 1 = 1/ρ at every stage (Proposition 3.1; misconception 2).
